# ES8311 codec driver tests

Exercises the ES8311 driver against a recording MCU platform that answers as
the codec and a full-duplex I2S link do. For the Output: identification, the
reset and power-up transcript, the clock program for both slot widths,
configure's refusals and reconfiguration, a pending run kept through zero and
partial acceptance and through an error, the Stream read only when nothing is
pending, each sample in both slots, silence reported as underrun, position,
pending, stop, restart, and sleep. For the Input: the microphone's transcript
and gain, capture only after start, either slot, thirty-two-bit words
narrowed, never taking more than the Stream holds, receiver drops reported as
overrun, errors, stop and restart. And one chip shared by both: one reset, one
link, one rate. The transmitter sends a frame only when a case ticks it and the
receiver receives one only when a case feeds it. No hardware is involved.
